          <h2>Rebar-Reinforced Concrete</h2>
          <p>Rebar-reinforced concrete has long been a trusted method for court foundations. By embedding steel bars (rebar) in the concrete slab, it provides added structural strength and has been used successfully in countless residential court projects. When built on stable soil, rebar slabs offer a solid foundation for pickleball, basketball, or tennis courts.</p>
          
          <h3>Key Benefits:</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Steel reinforcement adds structural support</li>
            <li>A widely used method in residential court building</li>
            <li>Straightforward construction with well-known materials</li>
          </ul>
          
          <div class="benefit-callout" style="margin-top: 2rem; padding: 1.5rem; background: #f0f4ff; border-left: 4px solid var(--primary, #2563eb); border-radius: 0.5rem;">
            <h4>Why Consider Post-Tension?</h4>
            <p>While rebar works well, sport courts are large, continuous slabs that need to maintain perfect flatness over time. Post-tension concrete is engineered to handle those demands, minimizing movement and maximizing the court's longevity. For many court projects, post-tension is the preferred solution for top-tier performance.</p>
          </div>
          
