          <span class="section-label">Right Choice When</span>
          <h2>Is Rebar Right for Your Project?</h2>
          <p>Rebar concrete is the perfect choice for many court projects, but understanding when it's the right fit helps ensure long-term success.</p>
          
          <h3>Ideal Conditions:</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Stable soil conditions with minimal expansion/contraction</li>
            <li>Proper drainage around the court area</li>
            <li>Residential or moderate-use commercial courts</li>
            <li>Projects with standard timelines and budgets</li>
            <li>Areas with mild to moderate freeze-thaw cycles</li>
          </ul>
          
          <h3>Consider Post-Tension When:</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Expansive clay soils are present</li>
            <li>Large court areas (tennis court or larger)</li>
            <li>Heavy use commercial installations</li>
            <li>Extreme weather conditions</li>
            <li>Premium crack-resistance is critical</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

